                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Salutary Complexity/Subversive Clarity",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                1092,
                530,
                1119
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 14,
            "global_block_id": 14,
            "global_group_id": 14,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    1092.0
                ],
                [
                    530.0,
                    1092.0
                ],
                [
                    530.0,
                    1119.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    1119.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "There are two more defenses of complexity: one is that complexity is good for us, the other is that clarity is bad.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                1127,
                782,
                1176
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 14,
            "group_id": 15,
            "global_block_id": 15,
            "global_group_id": 15,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    1127.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    1127.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    1176.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    1176.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "As to the first claim, some argue that the harder we have to work to grasp what we read, the more deeply we think and the better we understand. Everyone",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                1179,
                784,
                1229
            ],
